+Realtime Smoke Volume (Ex1604) is a hybrid rendering technique that combines low-resolution velocity projection with high-resolution density advection to visualize smoke in real-time [S1]. It solves the performance bottleneck of simulating and rendering dense volumetric smoke by decoupling the fluid dynamics resolution from the visual density resolution [S1]. Unlike its sibling [MacCormack Advection Scheme](4952-maccormack-advection-scheme.md), it explicitly separates the velocity projection resolution from the density advection resolution, and it builds on the tracking approach of [Smoke Advection](4639-smoke-advection.md) by ray marching the density in a volume pixel shader [S1].
 
